  "final_text": "I created the dashboard and the alert rule, and the rule is enabled. Its first run finished without errors and raised no alerts.\n\n**1. What the data holds.** The `Kibana Sample Data Logs` data view (index `kibana_sample_data_logs`, time field `timestamp`) is a log of individual web requests. Each record has:\n- **Response code** (`response`, stored as text with a `response.keyword` version)\n- **Size** (`bytes`)\n- **Visitor** (`clientip`)\n- **Request details** (`url`, `request`, `extension`, `referer`)\n- **Visitor context** (`geo.src`/`geo.dest`/`geo.coordinates`, `machine.os`, `agent`)\n- **Host and tags**\n\n**2. Dashboard `EFF-fcbf28c4 Web logs overview`** (id `2afb99eb-56d2-4cb1-af56-bcc279f4f7e6`, default time range last 7 days). It has 8 panels:\n- **Headline numbers:** Total requests, Unique visitors (distinct client IPs), Average bytes per request, and Error rate (percentage of 4xx/5xx responses)\n- Requests over time, stacked by response code\n- Requests by response code (donut chart)\n- Bytes transferred over time\n- Top 10 requested URLs, with request count and average bytes\n\nKibana accepted all 8 panels and they're stored. Five panels use ES|QL queries: error rate, the two over-time charts, the top-URLs table and the response-code donut. I couldn't test-run those queries because this Kibana blocks the console endpoint. They use standard syntax, but it's worth opening the dashboard once to confirm they show data.\n\n**3. Rule `EFF-fcbf28c4 5xx spike`** (id `2556ac20-4fa7-4ec2-a951-08aa0e889cba`):\n- It's an Elasticsearch query rule on `kibana_sample_data_logs` that runs every minute.\n- It counts requests whose response code starts with `5` (a prefix match on `response.keyword`) over the last 5 minutes, and fires when the count is more than 10.\n- It counts every request in the 5-minute window each time it runs, including ones already counted in earlier runs. This keeps the count a true 5-minute total.\n- No actions or connectors are attached, so a firing alert appears in Kibana but doesn't notify anyone. Add a connector if you want email or Slack messages.",
